# Sinfonia 15 in B minor, BWV 801 (9/16, 38 bars plus a longer last chord)
#
# Character: a lively gigue in 9/16. The subject is a pedal figure
# (b-fis-fis, g-fis-fis, b-fis-fis), then a thirty-second arpeggio
# sweeping down; the countersubject is a running sixteenth line. In
# bar 32 Bach writes a fermata on a dominant seventh, a dramatic halt
# before the last statement.
#
# Tempo: dotted eighth = 72 (three to the bar), about 1:40.
# Basis: Andras Schiff (ECM, clavichord) 1:29, about 77 dotted eighths
# a minute; Angela Hewitt (Hyperion, 1994) 1:38, about 70; Glenn Gould
# (1964) 1:04, about 108, much faster and not followed. Taken near
# Hewitt so the thirty-second arpeggios stay clean on the chip.
# Durations from retailer and artist track lists, so approximate.
#
# Structure (from the Mutopia score):
#   1-3    Subject in the top, B minor, countersubject in the bass.
#   4-6    Subject in the bass, countersubject in the top (the two
#          parts swap).
#   7-13   Mid enters with the head (7); the head then falls through a
#          sequence of keys, top and mid in turn (E, A, D).
#   14     Cadence in D major; subject in the mid (14-16), heading to A.
#   17-19  Subject in the top, A major; cadence in E minor, bar 20.
#   20-25  Second falling sequence of the head, mid and top in turn,
#          back to B minor, bar 26.
#   26-29  Arpeggio sequence over a falling bass, to F-sharp.
#   30-32  B minor, then E held in the bass (31-32) under a dominant
#          seventh: fermata in bar 32.
#   33-38  Arpeggio, then the final cadence (trill) in B minor; the
#          last chord is a held, fermata B minor.

tempo 72 8.           # dotted eighth, see above
accent 1              # gigue: a light lift on each downbeat

dyn 1 mf              # bars 1-6: exposition
lead 1-2 top          # bars 1-2: subject in the top
lead 4-5 bottom       # bars 4-5: subject in the bass

dyn 7 mp              # bars 7-13: first sequence, a lighter manual
lead 7-8 mid          # bars 7-8: the mid voice enters with the head

dyn 14 mf             # bars 14-19: after the D major cadence
lead 14-15 mid        # bars 14-15: subject in the mid, D major
lead 17-18 top        # bars 17-18: subject in the top, A major

dyn 20 mp             # bars 20-25: second sequence, an echo of the first

dyn 26 mf             # bars 26-30: back in B minor, arpeggio sequence
ramp 27-31 f          # bars 27-31: build into the dominant seventh
broaden 31 0.9        # bar 31: hold back into the fermata
broaden 32 0.5        # bar 32: Bach's fermata, roughly doubling the bar

dyn 33 mf             # bars 33-38: after the pause, the closing statement
rit 3 0.7             # last 3 bars into the final B minor chord
